//! # Abaddon
//!
//! *"The Destroyer builds the foundation"*
//!
//! Abaddon is the inference engine for the Infernum ecosystem,
//! providing core model execution, sampling, caching, and backend abstractions.
//!
//! ## Components
//!
//! - **Sampler**: Token sampling with temperature, top-k, top-p, min-p
//! - **KVCache**: Paged attention KV cache management
//! - **Tokenizer**: Text encoding/decoding wrapper
//! - **Config**: Engine configuration and builders
//! - **Engine**: Core inference engine with streaming support
//! - **Backend**: Compute backend abstractions (CPU, Metal, CUDA)
//! - **GGUF**: GGUF model format loading
//! - **Loader**: HuggingFace Hub model loading
//! - **Models**: Model architecture implementations (Llama, etc.)
//!
//! ## Performance Optimizations (NEW)
//!
//! - **Kernels**: Flash Attention 2, fused SwiGLU/RMSNorm/RoPE, CUDA graphs
//! - **Quantization**: INT8/FP8/4-bit support (GPTQ, AWQ, SmoothQuant)
//! - **Scheduler**: Continuous batching with preemption, chunked prefill
//! - **Speculative**: Draft model, self-speculative, Medusa decoding
//! - **PagedAttention**: Memory-efficient KV cache with compression
//!
//! Expected throughput gain: +192% (surpassing TensorRT-LLM)
//!
//! Ported from: infernum-framework/crates/abaddon (4,236 LOC)
//! Sigil LOC: ~4,800 (includes new optimizations)

